[19:12:09] STORY-WEB-024 is complete. Summary of what I did:
[19:12:09] **What changed** — five files. `discovery-browser-smoke.mjs` already carried the maintainer's own reconciliation of its control-group and inventory-selector steps in the working tree; that work is preserved and I only repaired the two stale steps below it.
[19:12:09] - **AC 1, layout** — the `synchronization` readiness selector waited for `[data-test="sync-controls"]`, which `SyncScreen.vue` doesn't render. It now waits for the price-cache health badge in the state the supplied status produces (the hook and tone class `SyncScreen.spec.ts` asserts), with the stub answering `/api/system/status`. Two further blockers appeared past that wait: the `page intro` contrast pair was being measured on an area with no intro (moved to `discovery`), and `BankScreen.vue`/`MaterialsScreen.vue` render their own `<h1>` without the `tabindex="-1" data-page-heading data-test="page-heading"` hooks, so `App.vue:56`'s post-navigation focus was a no-op there. I added those three attributes to the two headings — restoring the shell's existing behavior — and nothing else in either file.
